## ⚠️ CRITICAL: SQLite in Tests
**Always use `:memory:` for SQLite databases in tests.**
```go
db, err := sql.Open("sqlite3", ":memory:")  // ✅ Correct
// db, err := sql.Open("sqlite3", "linkshelf.db")  // ❌ WRONG - causes lock conflicts
```
If a test creates a SQLite database, it MUST use `:memory:` or `filepath.Join(t.TempDir(), "test.db")`. Never use file-based SQLite databases (like `linkshelf.db`) in tests — they cause locking conflicts when tests run in parallel or alongside a running server.

